        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Identify the payload"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771312214822"
          },
          "code": "IDENTIFY_THE_PAYLOAD",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772037598825",
          "id": "1771311494337",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771311494338_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Provided with the available fields for the opportunity, generate the payload to get the opportunity data required to answer the user query.\n\nUser Query: `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`\n\nFields: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_OPPORTUNITY_FIELDS.$output}}`\n\nThe payload must always include enough fields to identify each opportunity row. Always include:\n- Opportunity name attribute\n- Opportunity ID attribute, specifically `OptyId`\n\nIf the user query requires aggregation, totals, ranking, grouping, filtering, or comparison, still return row-level opportunity data with the required fields. The downstream answer-generation prompt will aggregate the row-level data as needed.\n\nSample payload:\n`{\"entity\":\"Opportunity\",\"q\":{\"op\":\"$and\",\"criteria\":[{\"op\":\"$in\",\"attribute\":\"StatusCode\",\"values\":[\"OPEN\"]},{\"op\":\"$or\",\"criteria\":[{\"op\":\"$eq\",\"attribute\":\"RecordSet\",\"value\":\"ORA_MYOPTIES\"},{\"op\":\"$eq\",\"attribute\":\"RecordSet\",\"value\":\"ORA_MYSUBORDINATESOPTIES\"}]}]},\"sort\":[{\"attribute\":\"EffectiveDate\",\"direction\":\"descending\"}],\"language\":\"en\",\"copiedFrom\":\"Opportunity\",\"limit\":15}`\n\nRules for payload generation:\n\n1. Field Selection\n- Use the field value from Fields metadata.\n- Never use the `displayLabel` field, as it may differ or change in the future.\n- Always include the opportunity name field in the output fields.\n- Always include `OptyId` in the output fields.\n- Include any additional fields required to answer the user query, such as amount, close date, status, owner, account, stage, forecast category, or effective date.\n- If the query asks for totals, counts, averages, grouping, comparison, ranking, or pipeline summaries, include the row-level fields needed for the calculation instead of returning only a pre-aggregated result.\n- Do not omit `OptyId`, even when the query appears to ask only for a summary.\n\n2. Filter Operators\n- Use the `attributeType` from Fields to decide which operators are valid.\n- Do not invent operators.\n- If type is unknown, allow only `[\"$in\",\"$notin\"]`.\n\nMapping:\n- Boolean -> `[\"$in\",\"$notin\"]`\n- Enum -> `[\"$in\",\"$notin\",\"$all\",\"$any\",\"$none\",\"$fm\"]`\n- Text / String -> `[\"$co\",\"$sw\",\"$ew\",\"$in\",\"$notin\",\"$all\",\"$any\",\"$none\",\"$fm\",\"$pr\",\"$npr\"]`\n- Long / Integer / BigDecimal / Currency / Percentage -> `[\"$gt\",\"$ge\",\"$lt\",\"$le\",\"$in\",\"$notin\",\"$wi\",\"$pr\",\"$npr\"]`\n- Date / Timestamp -> `[\"$gt\",\"$ge\",\"$lt\",\"$le\",\"$in\",\"$notin\",\"$wi\",\"$pr\",\"$npr\"]`\n- Record -> `[\"$co\",\"$sw\",\"$ew\",\"$in\",\"$notin\",\"$fm\",\"$pr\",\"$npr\",\"$eq\"]`\n\n- For ForeignKey fields where `attributeType = ForeignKey`, use the `$all` operator with a keyword or partial value:\n`{ \"operator\": \"$all\", \"value\": \"keyword\" }`\n- For `RecordSet` attribute, always use only `$eq`.\n\n3. Calendar Handling\n- Use the fiscal calendar only if the user explicitly mentions 'fiscal year', 'fiscal quarter', 'enterprise calendar', or similar terms.\n- If no fiscal context is mentioned, default to the Gregorian calendar.\n\n4. Fiscal Quarter Mapping\nWhen the user references fiscal quarters, apply this static mapping:\n- Q1: 6/1 to 8/31\n- Q2: 9/1 to 11/30\n- Q3: 12/1 to 2/28\n- Q4: 3/1 to 5/31\n\nUse this mapping to define appropriate `value1` and `value2` in date filters if the user requests a report by fiscal quarter.\n\n5. Strict Instructions for Relative Date Expressions\n- You must only use these units:\n  - `now/d` for days\n  - `now/M` for months\n  - `now/y` for years\n- You are forbidden from using `quarter`, `Q`, or `q` in any form in your output except for 'This Quarter'.\n- For 'This Quarter', use:\n  - `value1: \"now/q\"`\n  - `value2: \"now/q+1q\"`\n- If the input mentions quarters, convert quarters to months or years.\n- 1 quarter = 3 months.\n- 4 quarters = 1 year.\n- If the query says 'last N quarters', output:\n  - `value1: \"now/M\"`\n  - `value2: \"now/M-(N*3)M\"`\n- If the query says 'next N quarters', output:\n  - `value1: \"now/M+(N*3)M\"`\n  - `value2: \"now/M\"`\n- If your output contains `quarter`, `Q`, or `q` except for 'This Quarter', it is wrong and must be fixed.\n- Do not explain or mention quarters in the output.\n\nExamples:\n- Last 10 quarters -> `value1: \"now/M\"`, `value2: \"now/M-30M\"`\n- Last 4 quarters -> `value1: \"now/M\"`, `value2: \"now/M-12M\"`\n- Next 2 quarters -> `value1: \"now/M+6M\"`, `value2: \"now/M\"`\n- This Quarter -> `value1: \"now/q\"`, `value2: \"now/q+1q\"`\n- This Year -> `value1: \"now/y\"`, `value2: \"now/y+1y\"`\n- Last Year -> `value1: \"now/y-1y\"`, `value2: \"now/y\"`\n\nReturn only the JSON payload. Do not include explanations, Markdown, titles, or code fences."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "\"filterNode\": {\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\"op\", \"attribute\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"op\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"$eq\",\n        \"$co\",\n        \"$sw\",\n        \"$ew\",\n        \"$in\",\n        \"$notin\",\n        \"$all\",\n        \"$any\",\n        \"$none\",\n        \"$fm\",\n        \"$pr\",\n        \"$npr\",\n        \"$gt\",\n        \"$ge\",\n        \"$lt\",\n        \"$le\",\n        \"$wi\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"attribute\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"value\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"number\", \"integer\", \"boolean\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"values\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": [\"string\", \"number\", \"integer\", \"boolean\"]\n      },\n      \"minItems\": 1\n    },\n    \"value1\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"number\", \"integer\"]\n    },\n    \"value2\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"number\", \"integer\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"allOf\": [\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"enum\": [\"$gt\", \"$ge\", \"$lt\", \"$le\", \"$eq\", \"$co\", \"$sw\", \"$ew\", \"$all\", \"$any\", \"$none\", \"$fm\"]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"op\"]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\"value\"],\n        \"not\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            { \"required\": [\"values\"] },\n            { \"required\": [\"value1\"] },\n            { \"required\": [\"value2\"] }\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"enum\": [\"$in\", \"$notin\"]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"op\"]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\"values\"],\n        \"not\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            { \"required\": [\"value\"] },\n            { \"required\": [\"value1\"] },\n            { \"required\": [\"value2\"] }\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"const\": \"$wi\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"op\"]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"required\": [\"value1\", \"value2\"],\n        \"not\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            { \"required\": [\"value\"] },\n            { \"required\": [\"values\"] }\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"if\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"op\": {\n            \"enum\": [\"$pr\", \"$npr\"]\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"op\"]\n      },\n      \"then\": {\n        \"not\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            { \"required\": [\"value\"] },\n            { \"required\": [\"values\"] },\n            { \"required\": [\"value1\"] },\n            { \"required\": [\"value2\"] }\n          ]\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
