                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Format Response"
                  },
                  "diagram": {
                    "x": 7605.953350681658,
                    "y": 5669.693945029187
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1778952802483"
                  },
                  "id": "1778952714717",
                  "code": "FORMAT_RESPONSE",
                  "type": "LLM",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1778952714717_prompt",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "Provided with the user query `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}` and opportunity data `{{$context.$input.data}} `.\n\nAnalyze the opportunity data and answer the user's query directly.\n\nThe opportunity data may be returned as row-level data because each row includes opportunity name and `OptyId`. If the user query asks for a summary, total, count, average, grouping, ranking, comparison, or pipeline-level answer, aggregate the row-level opportunity data as needed before answering.\n\nExamples:\n- If the user asks for total pipeline, sum the relevant opportunity amount field.\n- If the user asks how many opportunities exist, count the opportunity rows.\n- If the user asks for opportunities by stage, group the rows by stage.\n- If the user asks for top opportunities, rank the rows by the relevant amount or date field.\n- If the user asks for this quarter's pipeline, use the returned filtered rows and aggregate the pipeline amount.\n\nIf the returned data contains **more than 5 rows, return top5 sorted on the most logical attribute**, include each opportunity in the response with an `action` property using this format:\n\n`ora.Invoke(\"launchOpportunity\", {\"opportunityId\":\"\"+<opportunityId>})`\n\n**Note** launchOpportunity is the key word and should not be changed at all.\n\nReplace `<opportunityId>` with the corresponding `opportunity.OptyId` value for that opportunity.\n\nIf more than 5 opportunities are returned, prioritize a summarized answer. Include individual opportunity details only when needed to answer the user query clearly.\n\nReturn the output in Markdown without code fences.\n\nFormatting rules:\n- Do not include a title.\n- Do not include classifications.\n- Start with a clear answer section.\n- Use bold for key values or important points where helpful.\n- Then include exactly one section heading named `Additional insights`.\n- Under `Additional insights`, provide concise bullet-point insights.\n- If opportunities are listed, include useful details such as opportunity name, amount, close date, and the `action` property.\n- Do not expose raw JSON unless it is specifically requested by the user.\n\nExample question:\n\nWhat is my total pipeline for this quarter?\n\nExample answer:\n\n**Answer**\n\nYou have **4 opportunities** with a total pipeline amount of **$240,000**.\n\n| Opportunity Name | Amount | action |\n|---|---:|---|\n| Abc | $60,000 | `ora.Invoke(\"launchOpportunity\", {\"opportunityId\":\"\"+\"300100001\"})` |\n| ACD | $50,000 | `ora.Invoke(\"launchOpportunity\", {\"opportunityId\":\"\"+\"300100002\"})` |\n| AFG | $60,000 | `ora.Invoke(\"launchOpportunity\", {\"opportunityId\":\"\"+\"300100003\"})` |\n| GTY | $70,000 | `ora.Invoke(\"launchOpportunity\", {\"opportunityId\":\"\"+\"300100004\"})` |\n\nAdditional insights\n- Opportunity Abc has an expected close date of **12 Jun** and needs immediate attention."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
